# Credentials for the seed script and for local Supabase work.
#
# SETUP:  cp supabase/.env.example supabase/.env  and fill in the two values.
#
# supabase/.env is gitignored. This example file is the only one committed.
# Nothing here is ever compiled into the app: the phone uses the anon key from
# Config.xcconfig, and the service role key exists only on your machine and
# inside the Edge Function's environment.

# Your project REST URL, from Settings > API in the Supabase dashboard.
SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co

# The service role key, from the same page.
#
# This key bypasses row level security completely. It can read and write every
# table in the project. Treat it like a root password: never commit it, never
# put it in the iOS app, never paste it into a browser console.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=YOUR-SERVICE-ROLE-KEY

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# For the nightly schedule (optional here, required in the database)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# pg_cron reads these from Supabase Vault, not from this file. Store them once
# against your project, using the same two values as above:
#
#   select vault.create_secret('https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co', 'project_url');
#   select vault.create_secret('YOUR-SERVICE-ROLE-KEY',                'service_role_key');
#
# Until you do, the nightly job fires and fails harmlessly, and every country
# shows a last_sync_error. Seeding by hand still works.
